$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247200 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247200 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111076" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247200 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247200 #edb/ref 1071 "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=4\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247200 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed526ede-6ba9-5979-b07c-e565cdc8a6e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247200 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>4) & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(2,5),(4,1),(4,3),(4,5)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,5))+P((X,Y)=(4,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(4,3))+P((X,Y)=(4,5)) \\\\  & =f(2,5)+f(4,1)+f(4,3)+f(4,5) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247203 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247203 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111081" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247203 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247203 #edb/ref 1071 "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.06$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.04$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(X>1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=0)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247203 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7b0070a7-d639-52f6-9076-6af2ae611dd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247203 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,